## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design end-to-end, production-grade guardrails for cross-tenant deployments in Azure, focusing on identity, secret management, policy gates, canaries, and UEBA automation.

## Key Concepts
- Workload identities and Just-In-Time access
- Azure Key Vault with per-service managed identities
- Azure Policy gates to block secrets in config
- Azure Lighthouse for cross-tenant governance
- Canary deployments with feature flags and automatic rollback
- UEBA via Azure Sentinel with automated playbooks

## Code Example
```json
{
  "policyRule": {
    "if": {
      "field": "type",
      "in": ["Microsoft.Web/sites", "Microsoft.AzureFunctionsJobHost"]
    },
    "then": {
      "effect": "auditIfNotExists",
      "details": {
        "type": "Microsoft.KeyVault/vaults/secrets"
      }
    }
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test the policy in a non-prod environment?
- What metrics trigger the automated rollback and how are they evaluated?

## Why This Is Asked
Demonstrates practical understanding of basic Azure security controls: private networking, secret management, and policy enforcement in a real-world setup.

## Key Concepts
- Private Endpoints and Storage Account network rules
- Azure Policy to deny public access on storage and require private endpoints
- Key Vault references for secrets in App Settings
- Lightweight rollback and validation in CI/CD

