## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test rollback if private endpoints fail to provision?
- What are the trade-offs of denying public access vs. private endpoints in a multi-region setup?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests knowledge of zero-trust, cross-tenant governance, and service mesh integration in Azure for multi-tenant SaaS with minimal network churn. It probes practical decisions around identity, cryptography, and policy enforcement.

## Key Concepts
- Azure AD workload identity for Kubernetes
- Istio mTLS and certificate management
- Private Endpoints for data plane isolation
- ABAC with policy-based access control
- Azure Policy and Lighthouse for cross-tenant governance

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo: validate that a service has a binding token from AD and that mTLS certs are valid
async function authorizeCall(service, peer) {
  const token = await fetchAzureAdToken(service);
  const cert = await getMTLSCert(peer);
  if (!token || !verifyCert(cert)) throw new Error('Unauthorized');
  if (!policyAllows(service, peer)) throw new Error('Policy denied');
  return true;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you monitor and alert on policy violations across tenants?
- What rollback criteria would you implement for a failed rollout?

## Why This Is Asked

Probes automated containment and rollback for cross-region, multi-tenant Azure SaaS. Emphasizes real-time orchestration across Key Vault, AAD, RBAC, canaries, and traffic routing.

## Key Concepts

- Defender for Cloud UEBA integrations
- Event Grid and Logic Apps for automation
- Per-tenant Key Vault key rotation and token revocation
- Tenant isolation via RBAC and traffic redirection
- Canary controls and sandbox forensics

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo handler for UEBA alert
async function handleUEBAAlert(event) {
  const id = event.tenantId;
  await rotateTenantKeys(id);
  await revokeTenantTokens(id);
  await setTenantRBAC(id, 'read-only');
  await pauseCanariesForTenant(id);
  await redirectTraffic(id, 'lastKnownGood');
  await cloneTenantSandbox(id);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you test this workflow end-to-end?
- How would you audit changes made during containment?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical guardrail implementation and rollback in Azure, focusing on private endpoints and storage exposure controls.

## Key Concepts
- Azure Policy initiatives
- Private Endpoint and Private DNS for SQL
- Storage account publicNetworkAccess controls
- Post-deploy validation and rapid rollback

## Code Example
```javascript
// Post-deploy validation sketch (Node.js)
const { DefaultAzureCredential } = require("@azure/identity");
const { StorageManagementClient } = require("@azure/arm-storage");
const credential = new DefaultAzureCredential();
const subscriptionId = "<sub-id>";
const client = new StorageManagementClient(credential, subscriptionId);
async function checkStoragePublicAccess(rg, name) {
  const acc = await client.storageAccounts.getProperties(rg, name);
  return acc?.properties?.networkAcls?.publicNetworkAccess !== "Enabled";
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test this in a dev environment before production rollout?
- What logs/alerts would you configure to catch violations early, and how would you automate rollback if the last-good template isn’t found?

## Why This Is Asked

Interview context explanation.

## Key Concepts

- Azure AD PIM and per-service managed identities
- Azure Key Vault secret management and rotation
- Azure Policy to prevent secrets in config and enforce KV references
- Canary deployments and feature flags (App Configuration)
- Rollback strategies and monitoring (Azure Monitor, Activity Logs)

## Code Example

```javascript
const { DefaultAzureCredential } = require("@azure/identity");
const { SecretClient } = require("@azure/keyvault-secrets");
const credential = new DefaultAzureCredential();
const kv = new SecretClient(process.env.KEY_VAULT_URI, credential);
async function getSecret(name) {
  const s = await kv.getSecret(name);
  return s.value;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you validate that no secrets exist in App Service configurations across all environments?
- How would you test the rollback path under production load?
